# -*- mode: snippet -*-
# name: reading-session
# key: rsession
# --
** [`(format-time-string "%Y-%m-%d %a")`]
*** Scope:
:GUIDE:
What you read — chapter, section, pages.
The session date records when you read. You can complete Summary, Reflection, and Questions later.
:END:
*** Notes
:GUIDE:
Your workspace while reading.
- Follow the text's headings when useful.
- Restate claims in your own words and explain how they connect.
- Add reactions, links, and inline Q: questions where they arise.
- Keep exact quotations distinct from your paraphrases. Include page or section references where useful.
- Distinguish what the text says from your interpretation and outside explanations. Mark uncertain claims, including AI explanations, for checking.

Write here directly. Notes do not need to begin as Readwise highlights.
Use Readwise for passages you want to see again in daily review, not as a required copy of these notes.
:END:
*** Summary
:GUIDE:
After the reading chunk, summarize from memory with the text and your notes out of view.
Explain the main claims and how they connect. Describe the author's argument, not your assessment of it.
Use prose or an outline. Let the material determine the length; do not reproduce every reading note.
Then check the text and your notes. Correct errors and fill important gaps.
This can happen later, not necessarily in the same sitting as reading.
:END:
*** Reflection
:GUIDE:
Review your notes and revisit unclear passages.
Answer inline questions where the text resolves them.

Add what this second look reveals:
- What changed in your understanding?
- What connections or disagreements now seem important?
- What do you still find unclear, and why?

Do not copy reactions already recorded under Notes. Refer back to them or develop them further.
Leave this section empty if the review adds nothing.
:END:
*** Questions
:GUIDE:
Keep questions that remain after review as STUDY headings beneath this heading.
They can come from Notes, Reflection, or gaps exposed by the Summary.
State each question clearly enough that future-you understands the difficulty.

Before the next session, review earlier open questions.
When the text answers one, mark it DONE. Add a short answer and a passage reference.
Update an existing concept node if the answer adds useful understanding.

At book completion, review the remaining questions.
Promote questions worth pursuing beyond the book into new or existing zk question nodes.
Add a linked STUDY entry in projects.org to keep that work visible.
Leave book-specific uncertainties here unless they warrant further study.
Not every unanswered question needs a node.
:END:
